A||||5||Turbo88||Cat removal||||1||
Z||000000||Turbo88||09-18-2001||10:02 PM||||For those of you that have removed your catalytic converters or had them gutted, what modifications did you have to do to the ECM or O2 sensors? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||v8fieroGT||09-18-2001||10:18 PM||||I removed mine on my gt and se. All i did was cut off the cat with a sawsall and bough a piipe from a local car parts store that fit snuggly on both ends and clamped it with exaust clamps. I didn't do any other motifications to any sensors.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Turbo88||09-18-2001||10:49 PM||||Ahh I see what the deal is. I'm still in the LS1 mindset (latest project <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">). The fiero's ecm only uses one 02 sensor and it is  before the cat. Some computers use two, one before and one after to monitor the combustion of excess fuel by the cat. Sinse there is only one 02 sensor, it only monitors exhaust as it leaves the engine and depends on the cat to remove it without any computer adjustments. <P>Cool! That simplifies things <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.. Thanks for the info!!!<P>-Bryan<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-19-2001||03:56 AM||||Get a new stainless cat from rodney. <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.rodneydickman.com</A> <P>The OEM cats are horrible, BUT rodney's is great. (completely different, flow rate is far higher) <P>Removing the cat entirely will actually cost you horsepower, compared to a new unit.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000004||Turbo88||09-19-2001||07:54 AM||||Well it will cost you back pressure, which costs you bottem end torque. But that's fine because in the low range, the turbine spinning at low rpm will cause some back pressure as well and will hopefully offset that. I am actually going to test with and without a cat inline and see where it helps me most. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||mshill||09-19-2001||05:51 PM||||Since my rebuild in Dec 1999 (stock 2.8 with a +1 cam) I have been running without a cat.  I had to get it CA smogged this month and put on a universal (AutoZone) cat.  Instantly, I noticed the exhaust was much quieter and I definitely cannot get up to 5500 RPM as fast as without it.  As soon as I get a pipe I'm taking it back off.  I don't think my cam likes the backpressure from the cat.||||reg||1
